// models/seeds.memql -- the curated set (epic memql#5137, D2).
//
// VERIFIED 2026-09-07 against the Ollama library pages, the Hugging Face model
// cards and the vendor announcements. The record says to re-verify every id and
// size before seeding because tags move, and two had:
//
//   - `parakeet-tdt-1.1b` (named in D2) no longer exists. NVIDIA's current
//     Parakeet is `parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3`, which is what is seeded. A profile
//     naming a tag the runtime does not serve fails at pull time with the
//     runtime's own error, which is a worse place to learn it than here.
//   - `gemma4:26b` is a 4B-active mixture, not the 3.8B-active the record says.
//
// Both corrections are carried back into the design record in this epic's PR,
// per the program record's rule 4.
//
// WHAT IS NOT SEEDED, AND WHY IT IS STILL NAMED. `fish-speech-1.5` is in D2's
// audioOut row and is seeded at its published id; FishAudio has since shipped
// S1 and S2, but the record names 1.5 and re-pointing a curated entry to a
// model nobody has run here is a curation decision rather than a verification
// one, so it stays and the note says so.
//
// sizeBytes IS LEFT AT ZERO where the publisher does not state a download size
// -- every non-Ollama entry. A zero reads as "not stated" on the page; an
// invented number reads exactly like a measured one, which is worse than a gap.

// =============================================================================
//   text -- the workhorses. Every one of these carries vision, tools, thinking
//   and structured output in a single record, which is the fact that makes a
//   small local model good enough for a harness that asks narrow questions.
// =============================================================================

